s="\"On a conjecture of Godsil concerning controllable random graphs (https://arxiv.org/abs/1511.05080)\\nciteturn1academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11.0 years ago; Title: On a conjecture of Godsil concerning controllable random graphs\\nAuthors: Sean O'Rourke, Behrouz Touri\\nTitle: On a conjecture of Godsil concerning controllable random graphs\\nAuthors: Sean O'Rourke, Behrouz Touri\\nDate: Mon Nov 16 18:37:21 2015\\n\\nIt is conjectured by Godsil that the relative number of controllable graphs compared to the total number of simple graphs on n vertices approaches one as n tends to infinity. We prove that this conjecture is true. More generally, our methods show that the linear system formed from the pair (W, b) is controllable for a large class of Wigner random matrices W and deterministic vectors b. The proof relies on recent advances in Littlewood-Offord theory developed by Rudelson and Vershynin.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nControllability of random systems: Universality and minimal controllability (https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.03125)\\nciteturn1academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11.4 years ago; Authors: Sean O'Rourke, Behrouz Touri ... For a large class of random matrices $A$ and vectors $b$, we show that linear systems formed from the pair $(A,b)$ are controllable with high probability.\\nTitle: Controllability of random systems: Universality and minimal controllability\\nAuthors: Sean O'Rourke, Behrouz Touri\\nDate: Tue Jun  9 22:48:28 2015\\n\\nFor a large class of random matrices $A$ and vectors $b$, we show that linear systems formed from the pair $(A,b)$ are controllable with high probability. Despite the fact that minimal controllability problems are, in general, NP-hard, we establish universality results for the minimal controllability of random systems. Our proof relies on the recent developments of Nguyen-Tao-Vu concerning gaps between eigenvalues of random matrices.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nLittlewood-Offord theory and controllability of random structures (https://experts.illinois.edu/en/publications/littlewood-offord-theory-and-controllability-of-random-structures/)\\nciteturn1search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.9 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; We show that, as the dimension of the state space goes to infinity, the probability of (A,b) being controllable approaches one for many choices of the vector b including elements of the standard basis, the all-one vector, and random binary vectors. ... O'Rourke, S & Touri, B 2016, Littlewood-Offord theory and controllability of random structures. in 2016 IEEE 55th Conference on Decision and Control, CDC 2016., 7799064, 2016 IEEE 55th Conference on Decision and Control, CDC 2016, Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc., pp. 5195-5200, 55th IEEE Conference on Decision and Control, CDC 2016, Las Vegas, United States, 12/12/16. https://doi.org/10.1109/CDC.2016.7799064\\n\\n# Littlewood-Offord theory and controllability of random structures\\n\\n  * Sean O'Rourke\\n  * , Behrouz Touri\\n\\nResearch output: Chapter in Book/Report/Conference proceeding › Conference contribution\\n\\n## Abstract\\n\\nMotivated by recent developments in random matrix theory through the study of inverse Littlewood-Offord problems, we investigate the controllability of random binary symmetric matrices. We show that, as the dimension of the state space goes to infinity, the probability of (A,b) being controllable approaches one for many choices of the vector b including elements of the standard basis, the all-one vector, and random binary vectors. In particular, we verify a conjecture of Godsil [1] and show that most systems are controllable from single inputs.\\n\\nOriginal language  | English (US)\\nTitle of host publication  | 2016 IEEE 55th Conference on Decision and Control, CDC 2016\\nPublisher  | Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.